        "raw": "<p>(There isn&#39;t really an appropriate forum to put this thread in as far as I can see; feel free to move it.)</p><p>So, here&#39;s the thing.&nbsp; Growing rapidly familiar with my Enhanced Edition set&#39;s Heroes and Environments and even the Villains a little, I&#39;d really like to give myself more options pretty soon.&nbsp; Since a friend of mine has Infernal Relics and Rook City, I&#39;m not especially committed to getting those, even if they weren&#39;t sold out (not that I *won&#39;t*, it&#39;s just a lower priority).&nbsp; But I definitely want to be sure that I acquire Shattered Timelines and the mini-expansions.</p><p>However, while I have no reluctance to give GTG my money in fairly substantial quantities, I don&#39;t really want to pay the $10.70 minimum shipping cost more than once; if at all possible, I want to be able to place one order for all the Sentinels product I plan on getting anytime soon, get it all in one box and not have to pay a huge freight surcharge on what is already $100+ worth of game (and I do mean worth, but still, the raw dollar amount is a concern given that I&#39;m between jobs and have a few bills I&#39;d prefer to keep paid).&nbsp; With the Vengeance expansion coming out at some point in the nearish future, I&#39;m debating whether I&#39;d like to wait for that before ordering.&nbsp; But at the same time, a) I&#39;m chomping at the bit to get my hands on Unity and Miss Information and the Time Cataclysm so that I can start enjoying four times the variety in my Sentinels gaming, and b) I don&#39;t want to risk that ST or the mini-expansions will sell out and leave me unable to get them.</p><p>So, my question is this: can I afford to wait for Vengeance to come out, or should I grab my intended product NOW and risk that when Vengence comes out, I may decide to go without it for a long while, rather than pay the $10.70 in shipping a second time?</p>",
